class:: MidSideRatio
summary:: Mid to side energy ratio in decibels
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Amplitude

description::
With M=(L+R)/2 and S=(L-R)/2, computes 10*log10((sum(M.squared)+1e-24)/(sum(S.squared)+1e-24)), limited to +/-120 dB. Positive values favor centre content and negative values favor side content.

Uses an exact rolling sample window, with output held at zero until it is full. The update cost is linear in the input block size, with a once-per-window sum rebase to bound roundoff drift. Memory is two windows of doubles, allocated at initialization. Formulas are independently implemented from energy, M/S decomposition, and Pearson correlation. Silence returns zero.

Vanilla Amplitude can track channel levels separately; this UGen directly relates the channels over a fixed shared interval.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: left
Left audio-rate input.

argument:: right
Right audio-rate input.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time rolling window, 0.001..2 seconds; default 0.05.

returns::
Mid/side ratio in dB; silence returns zero.

examples::
MidSideRatio computes the logarithmic power ratio between mid and side components in decibels (positive values indicate center-dominant mono energy; negative values indicate side-dominant wide energy). In this example, the mid/side ratio controls a dynamic spatial compressor, providing transparent acoustic stabilization across the stereo image. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time mid/side ratio in dB.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("stereo.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.isKindOf(Buffer) and: { ~miraBuffer.numChannels >= 2 }) {
            PlayBuf.ar(2, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
                var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1);
                [sig, DelayC.ar(sig, 0.02, 0.003)]
            } {
                // Synthetic stereo fallback
                var l = Saw.ar(220) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                var r = Saw.ar(222) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                [l, r]
            }
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]);

        var msRatio = MidSideRatio.kr(source[0], source[1], windowTime: 0.05);
        var msLag = msRatio.lag(0.08);
        var mid = (source[0] + source[1]) * 0.5;
        var side = (source[0] - source[1]) * 0.5;
        var sideBoost = msLag.linlin(0, 18, 1.3, 0.8).clip(0.5, 1.5);
        var sound = [mid + (side * sideBoost), mid - (side * sideBoost)] * 0.25;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, msLag.clip(-24, 24)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Mid/Side Ratio", ~miraBus, -18.0, 18.0, "dB");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
